── FACT BEYOND A `without` LIMIT ── E0204_assert_in_a_raising_function.lt:2:3  [E0204]

This `assert` can panic, but `withdraw` says `without panic`:

  1 │ pub fn withdraw(balance: i64, amount: i64) -> i64 / raise<str> without panic {
    │                                                                        ───── the limit
  2 │   assert amount <= balance
    │   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^

A `without` promises that the code, and everything it calls, never does what the
limit names. Change the code so that it can't, or remove the limit if the code
needs it.

To fix it, raise an error instead:

  2 │   if amount > balance { raise "assertion failed" }
    │   ~~~      ~~~       +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
